# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-7, 2.1-9, 2.1-11, E §4.2 Parts in the walk). L §3.6's example kind savings and its arrival
# rule civ_arrive, whole (community: the couple's; inherited: the heir's; moved: "m.cash.amount of p / m.cash.amount",
# the labels kept), and its leaving rule: "an outflow takes the couple's part first, and shares what is left in
# proportion". wage 1 000.00 (community), inh 500.00 (tomek's), spend 300.00 (from the couple's), mv 600.00 to konto2
# (the couple's 700.00 cover it; konto2's arrival keeps its label), spend2 400.00 (the couple's 100.00, then tomek's
# 300.00). L §5.10: bal(x, d) of q is "the sum of x's parts labelled q at the end of day d"; value(...) of q those parts
# at their prices (PLN at its amount); L §5.14 the leg read: what the leg took from q's parts. Figures by
# scratch/exp_a1.py.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind inheritances: transfers
  attr heir: key persons
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by civ_arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w v civ order (if k.owner == ania_tomek then 0 else 1) prorata ties by (if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1)
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place konto2: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input wage_day: date
input wage_amt: money PLN
input inh_day: date
input inh_amt: money PLN
input spend_day: date
input spend_amt: money PLN
input mv_day: date
input mv_amt: money PLN
input spend2_day: date
input spend2_amt: money PLN

def civ_arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule community = if p == ania_tomek then 1 else 0
  rule inherited beats community = if p == m.heir then 1 else 0 when m in inheritances
  rule moved beats community, inherited = m.cash.amount of p / m.cash.amount when m in transfers and m.cash.from in savings

move wage: transfers
  on wage_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount wage_amt
move inh: inheritances
  on inh_day
  attr heir = tomek
  leg cash from world to konto amount inh_amt
move spend: transfers
  on spend_day
  leg cash from konto to shop amount spend_amt
move mv: transfers
  on mv_day
  leg cash from konto to konto2 amount mv_amt
move spend2: transfers
  on spend2_day
  leg cash from konto to shop amount spend2_amt

ask q1: bal(konto, 2026-06-30), bal(konto, 2026-06-30) of ania_tomek, bal(konto, 2026-06-30) of tomek, bal(konto, 2026-06-30) of ania
ask q2: bal(konto2, 2026-06-30) of ania_tomek, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of tomek, value(konto, 2026-06-30) in PLN of tomek
ask q3: mv.cash.amount of ania_tomek, spend2.cash.amount of tomek

version civ
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[konto2] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  wage_day = 2026-02-01
  wage_amt = 1 000.00 PLN
  inh_day = 2026-03-01
  inh_amt = 500.00 PLN
  spend_day = 2026-04-01
  spend_amt = 300.00 PLN
  mv_day = 2026-05-01
  mv_amt = 600.00 PLN
  spend2_day = 2026-06-01
  spend2_amt = 400.00 PLN
=== expect
q1: (200.00 PLN, 0.00 PLN, 200.00 PLN, 0.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
q2: (600.00 PLN, 500.00 PLN, 200 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
q3: (600.00 PLN, 300.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
